WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.090
If your prep is MiraLAX, this video will walk you through exactly how to take

2
00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:04.240
it.

3
00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:06.560
Just follow along step by step.

4
00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:11.530
For this prep, you'll need a few items, all available over the counter, no

5
00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:12.000
prescription needed.

6
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.680
You'll need one 238-gram bottle of MiraLAX powder, two to four Dulcolax laxative

7
00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:19.360
tablets,

8
00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:25.040
and 64 ounces of a clear sports drink like Gatorade, Propel, or Crystal Light.

9
00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:30.640
That's usually two 32-ounce bottles. If you have diabetes, use sugar-free Gatorade

10
00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:31.200
G2.

11
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:36.160
Also, make sure you get the laxative tablets, not the stool softener.

12
00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:41.360
One important rule, your sports drink cannot be red, orange, blue, or purple.

13
00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:44.160
Stick to clear or light-colored flavors.

14
00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:49.440
The day before your colonoscopy, you'll start by mixing the solution.

15
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.990
Pour the entire bottle of MiraLAX into a pitcher with all 64 ounces of the

16
00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:55.760
sports drink.

17
00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:00.080
Stir or shake until the powder is completely dissolved.

18
00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:02.560
You can chill it in the refrigerator if you'd like.

19
00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:04.960
Keeping it cold makes it easier to drink.

20
00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:08.800
Now for part one, the evening before your procedure.

21
00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:13.600
At 4 p.m., take your Dulcolax tablets with a glass of water.

22
00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:17.200
Your doctor's instructions will tell you whether to take two or four.

23
00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:19.840
Follow their guidance on the specific amount.

24
00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:23.760
At 5 p.m., you'll start drinking the first half of the solution.

25
00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:25.520
That's 32 ounces.

26
00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:29.680
Drink an 8 ounce glass every 15 minutes until that half is gone.

27
00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:33.200
Keep drinking clear liquids after you finish.

28
00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:37.280
For part two, 6 hours before your colonoscopy,

29
00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:40.720
you'll drink the second half, which is another 32 ounces.

30
00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:45.440
Drink this at the same pace, an 8 ounce glass every 15 minutes.

31
00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:50.020
You can continue to have clear liquids up until four hours before your

32
00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:50.640
procedure.

33
00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:53.040
This part is really important.

34
00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:56.720
You must drink all of the prep solution as directed,

35
00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.880
even if you're already passing clear liquid.

36
00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:02.720
I know it can feel like enough, but finishing the entire dose

37
00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:05.360
is what gives us the clearest view during your procedure.

38
00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:09.840
If the prep isn't completed as directed, we may need to reschedule,

39
00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:11.280
and neither of us wants that.

40
00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:15.760
Please drink plenty of liquids throughout the process to prevent dehydration.

41
00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:20.480
Staying hydrated will help you feel better and help the prep do its job.

42
00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:24.880
If you experience any discomfort from frequent trips to the bathroom,

43
00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:29.360
applying a petroleum-based ointment or diaper rash cream can really help.

44
00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:30.720
That's it.

45
00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:32.160
You've got this.

46
00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:36.000
Follow the timing, finish the full dose, and stay hydrated.

47
00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:40.320
If you have any questions at all, don't hesitate to call our office.

48
00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:42.000
We're here to help.
